  "caption": "Quinn has never held a tennis racquet, yet after moving house even lifting a mug made the outer elbow zing. Three months of rest later, still sore.\n\nTennis elbow is an overloaded wrist-extensor tendon at the outer elbow, and it isn't just for tennis players. It can linger with pure rest or with repeated irritation, because tendons respond to the right kind of load.\n\nWhat can help: trim the biggest grip loads for now, try a counterforce strap for heavy tasks, build wrist-extensor and grip strength over weeks, strengthen the shoulder and have the neck checked, and plan in 8–12 week blocks.\n\nIf there's no improvement after months of a good program, get reassessed and talk with your GP.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
